d  scene from the first season the final  annie fight  back when everything was simpler the  time when aot had yet to show its full  repertoire in storytelling beats and  were all drawn to the tension-filled  survival battles against titans the ani  fight sets itself apart from the other  fights in this list and instead of  people fighting against the gigantic foe  we have aaron giving the good guys some  much needed firepower he goes toe to toe  with annie while the survey corpse all  work together to help subdue any once  and for all with how much more aot has  proven itself to be it's easy to  overlook this moment in the modern days  but back then this was an epic finale  for the smash hit the ears attack on  titan  [Music]  we can't leave fate out of this now can  we here's gorgon  you know i'm really tempted to put the  diamond fight here but i figured that i  talked about that fight enough and  wanted to give the spotlight to the  other giant boss fight in the series  gorgon the notable part about this fight  is how it happens early to show us an  idea of the villain's power at that  point we're led to believe that gorgon  is the diamond we've been hearing about  and her power certainly hints to them  leonidas and ushiwakamaru both tried  their best but even with their best shot  they're just no match hey at least they  made an epic show out of it though right  little did we know that things were  about to get worse especially when the  real theomath shows up we haven't seen  anything yet  princess connect makes its explosive  debut in these fight lists  princess connectors i've often described  it is wholesome konosuba it's very chill  less degenerate and is basically about a  group of friends having easy going  adventures together that is until stuff  starts getting real towards the end of  season one and parts of season two we  start uncovering a conspiracy and  learning the truth about the world and  yuki's memories oh and the fight scenes  for season two have been turned up a  notch and this fight is a prime example  of that the shadows give the characters  a chance to show off what they've got  and the golem leading them serves as the  big unbeatable obstacle that pushes them  in a race against time the whole thing  looks very well done and could have  caught people off guard not too  different from the kobayashi's dragon  maid fight if you remember that all that  finishing off with one of the most  breathtaking animation sequences of  pekkarine's finishing blow it certainly  looks ufo tables the way the scene was  done  here's something you probably haven't  predicted to see  legend of the millennium dragon's final  fight i believe deserves its spot on the  list what is legend of the millennium  dragon you ask well it's a 2011 film  that feels like one of the few  precursors to the time travel isakai  subgenre before it was cool boy travels  back in time and takes part in a war  between factions it's got the  traditional japanese aesthetic the  samurai and the demons and a whole lot  of mysticism it's also got some twists  that i won't call completely  unpredictable but hey it's there overall  i feel that the highlight of the movie  is the final battle going into more  details would be a spoiler but let's say  that it's a culmination on par with what  you'd expect out of this movie everyone  throwing what they have at the villain  the daunting atmosphere of the whole  thing and the finish brought about by  some help from the heavens if you've got  an hour and a half to burn and you're  into time travel fantasy it's a guy then  you should definitely try watching this  movie  speaking of fantasy why don't we check  out this dunmuchi moment  fantasy with some game mechanics a  gigantic boss fight feels completely at  home here the goliath fight in danmachi  is one of my favorite moments in the  show and it has a lot to do with the  whole build-up for comparison sakes  whereas the sao moment a while ago  dazzled us with cool visuals and  callbacks to erase that we loved this  one makes full use of the atmosphere the  tension it's really so hype seeing ryu  and bell fight together and the fight  has no shortage of drama pick a best  moment seriously is it the finishing  move or the number of tough sacrifices  done in this battle however if there's  anything to take away from the fight  it's the explanation for the sword it's  got some people questioning it but  that's just the thing with ellen  adaptations still even as an anime first  i really enjoyed this battle  next we go on to a slightly different  take of our ancient historical kingdoms  in muggy  margie's as a series is for me one of  the best shonen in the 2010s not even a  biased take and i feel that it's grossly  underrated considering how it  masterfully combines adventure action  politics and a whole lot of cool  character designs it's fitting that we  had one big raid boss fight to cap off  its anime run what i like about this  fight is that it really gives off the  aura of finality we know it's not the  final battle but with how over the top  everything is it provides a perfect  payoff to this anime we had almost all  named characters flowing in getting  their moments to show off yet ultimately  falling to off the medium it's one  dynamic entry after another culminating  with sinbad and the entire seven seas  alliance coming to the rescue it's a fun  ride that spanned a couple of episodes  and it just drives the magnitude of the  battle home  next is ores versus straw hats  when it comes to one piece fights we  often talk about those big one-on-one  fights however in a world where pretty  much anything's possible it's no  surprise that the straw hats would run  themselves into giant threats kaido is  one but i want to talk about the oars  fight it's a multi-part battle wherein  the straw hats take their fair share of  elves thanks to the immense power of  ores luffy soon joins the fight and even  then they find themselves in such a  pickup it took everything from the straw  hats to finally beat them and it felt  like such an earned victory with him no  selling everything episode after episode  him falling after that final giant  bazooka gave me the thrill of seeing a  raid boss finally fought in the video  games i played  next we have sao's final fight in  ordinal scale  it's no secret that i really like sao  now with this anime officially turning a  decade old in a short while a lot has  been said about the franchise a rather  uncommon opinion that i hold however is  that ordinal scale is somewhere up there  as one of the best sao anime that we've  got it's got everything you'd want from  a movie it builds on the acclaimed first  part of season 1 gives us a movie that's  generally self-contained and well paced  and of course finish off with what i  feel is the best boss fight the  franchise had you're talking the real  last boss of aincrad here a monstrosity  that not even kirito and friends could  beat on their own at first then everyone  from every game they played came in and  it was a real raid for the ages most of  the characters get their highlight shots  in and the kirito arsuna finish was just  perfect even if you've tuned out of sao  i still encourage you to watch this film  it recaptures the magic and condenses  everything in a nice movie with a mix of  everything drama action romance and some  fan service  that's got to do it for this list if you  have some giant fights that i've missed  then don't hesitate to tell me in the  comments actually you know what why stop  with just commenting i know comments are  good for the algorithm and i appreciate  that but i'd also invite you to come and  join us and hop on to our social media  whether it be the vini tube discord  channel instagram or patreon don't  forget to check out our sponsors of this  video lord of heroes the links in the  description thanks for watching and i  hope to see you next time stay safe stay  strong and stay awesome  you
 

